        "date": "2026-11-07T12:21:07Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): pick the GPU adapter by adapter, not only by backend, and log slow frames\n\nHybrid Intel UHD + NVIDIA laptops either landed on an adapter that never\nrendered or refused outright; the old chain varied only the backend mask\nand took wgpu's default-power adapter.\n\nChanges:\n- gpu_init.rs (new): per backend mask (preferred -> PRIMARY -> all),\n  enumerate every adapter and log each (name, vendor, device, type,\n  backend, presentable); try candidates one by one - request_device, a\n  capability-driven surface config, and a configure checked inside a\n  validation error scope + unwind guard. A failure logs its named reason\n  and moves to the next adapter; adapters that failed under an earlier\n  mask are not retried. When none works, the refusal names every adapter\n  tried and why, on stderr and in a native dialog (no silent window).\n- gpu_select.rs (new, pure): candidate order and surface config.\n  Order: the --gpu/CAMCRAFT_GPU named adapter -> the GPU wgpu's\n  PowerPreference::HighPerformance request answers with -> every other\n  presentable adapter, discrete > integrated > virtual > other > cpu;\n  ties go to the platform's native backend (DX12 on Windows, Metal on\n  macOS, Vulkan elsewhere), then enumeration order. Unpresentable\n  adapters are skipped by name.\n  Config: the surface's own first format, Fifo unless absent, Opaque\n  alpha when offered else the first reported mode (was get_default_config\n  + a hard-wired AutoVsync).\n- gpu.rs: `--gpu <name substring>` over `CAMCRAFT_GPU`, the same pattern\n  as --gpu-backend / CAMCRAFT_GPU_BACKEND; a valueless flag refuses.\n- frame_watch.rs (new) + shell draw: a frame over 100 ms is logged with\n  its phases (commands+scene, ui, acquire, encode, submit+present),\n  rate-limited to one line per 5 s.\n\nStall: not found headlessly. No blocking readback or device.poll(Wait)\nis on the idle frame path (readbacks are tests/diagnostics only; the\ntraced-stock eye marches only with Deviate/playback armed). The leading\nsuspect is Vulkan-on-Optimus cross-adapter presentation, which the\nnative-backend-first order avoids on Windows; the frame-time log pins\nthe phase from the reporter's machine.\n\nTests: gpu_select::tests (discrete_before_integrated_before_cpu,\nuser_choice_wins_case_insensitively, unmatched_choice_is_said_and_auto_order_stands,\nhigh_performance_pick_leads_on_its_best_backend,\nunpresentable_adapters_are_skipped_by_name, nothing_to_order_is_empty_not_a_panic,\nlog_line_names_every_field, config_comes_from_reported_capabilities,\nincompatible_surface_refuses_by_name), frame_watch::tests (3),\ngpu::tests::adapter_choice_flag_then_env.\n\nRefs #74\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
