      "message": "fix(ui): check GPU bring-up for OOM, internal errors and device loss; try the next adapter on a View3D failure\n\nPR #76 review fixes:\n- configure, the View3D build and one presented test frame run inside\n  Validation + OutOfMemory + Internal error scopes with a device-lost\n  callback and a bounded poll; any failure names the adapter and the\n  next one is tried (a lost device no longer passes as Ok)\n- the same GPU across backends matches on PCI vendor + device ids when\n  both are non-zero (name only otherwise), so DX12 keeps the HP rank\n- the refusal lists skipped adapters and empty backend masks instead of\n  \"no GPU adapter was found\"\n- the View3D pipeline is built per candidate: a failure drops that\n  adapter and tries the next instead of exiting with no dialog\n- --gpu=x / --gpu-backend=x parse; a surface-handle failure keeps the\n  failures collected so far; doc line on --gpu-backend narrowing --gpu\n- tests: same_gpu_named_differently_per_backend_still_leads_on_dx12,\n  refusal_names_tried_and_skipped_adapters, empty_alpha_modes_refuse_by_name,\n  caps_without_render_attachment_refuse_by_name, equals_form_flags_are_parsed\n\nRefs #74\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
